{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/617841-dread-presence-question","id":617841,"title":"Dread Presence question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-06T10:08:08-07:00","id":617841,"title":"Dread Presence question","content":"Does it inflict a condition? My copy of Blood &amp; Smoke doesn't mention one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T10:20:24-07:00","id":617866,"title":"","content":"Not by itself. It can be used in conjunction with the other levels to make oneself the source of a condition, strip away attributes, or increase the duration or area of effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T10:24:15-07:00","id":617868,"title":"","content":"No, but you could probably codify its effects into an Environmental Tilt if you wanted to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T13:12:57-07:00","id":618017,"title":"","content":"Trying work up a haunt version of ublette.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T14:46:41-07:00","id":618093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/617841-dread-presence-question?p=618017#post618017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying work up a haunt version of ublette.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case I would probably have the effects of Dread Presence affect everyone in the area. Turning it into an environmental Tilt would probably be the easiest way to do that, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T13:59:55-07:00","id":627896,"title":"","content":"I have actually been working on a Devotion for just that, looking a little something like this;<br /> <br /> Halls of Madness (Obfuscate 5, Nightmare 4)<br /> Cost: 5-12 Vitae, 1 Willpower<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Roll: None<br /> Duration: 1 week per Blood Potency<br /> Much like with the use of Oubliette, the Nosferatu marks their territory with their own Vitae. The amount of Vitae spent varies between five and twelve, depending on the size of the area they wish to mark. They then slumber. With these aspects, this Devotion seems very similar to the pinnacle of Obfuscate and indeed, a vampire that has marked an area with Halls of Madness benefits from all advantages of Oubliette. But this Devotion is so much more than that. It warps the vampire's territory, turning it... Surreal somehow. Like out of a bad dream. Shadows move when one traverses the Halls of Madness, a large figure brandishing a bloody knife can be seen, only for a second, only to disappear once one blinks. Faint laughter, or screams, can be heard echoing from far away. One opens a door and sees the inside of the room drenched in blood and recoils in horror, but it appears perfectly clean the next time they look. The Nosferatu may freely use Dread Presence, The Grand Delusion and Waking Nightmare on anyone inside the Halls of Madness. Furthermore, anyone that has spent more than a few minutes within Halls of Madness is on edge, nervous and jumpy. They suffer the Distracted Condition until they leave the area. Finally, if a mortal spends a full day and night in the Halls of Madness, she suffers an Integrity Breaking Point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4906-deraneo","name":"Deraneo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T08:22:05-07:00","id":628675,"title":"","content":"Good, but I would make it just Obfuscate 5, Nightmare 1. Basically, 3 XP to improve your Oubliette with the option of add <u>your</u> Nightmare powers.<br /> <br /> It seems like a good Devotion, but not something that should have greater cost and requisites than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T14:01:44-07:00","id":629056,"title":"","content":"Perhaps, though the intention of the Devotion was to not only add the option of Nightmare, but to also make the Oubliette rather surreal and unnerving by just being there, which seems to fall more under the purview of Waking Nightmare to me. Hence the Condition and Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> Perhaps two Devotions could be made, one requiring the other and adding those effects, but also requiring Nightmare 4? Three Experiences to get the Oubliette improvement and one or two Experiences to make the weirdness a more passive thing, complete with Condition and other effects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4906-deraneo","name":"Deraneo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T16:54:02-07:00","id":629202,"title":"","content":"I wasn't clear, sorry.<br /> <br /> Just reduce the requisites and cost. Let the Devotion precisely as you did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T10:14:33-07:00","id":632486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deraneo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/617841-dread-presence-question?p=627896#post627896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have actually been working on a Devotion for just that, looking a little something like this;<br /> <br /> Halls of Madness (Obfuscate 5, Nightmare 4)<br /> Cost: 5-12 Vitae, 1 Willpower<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Roll: None<br /> Duration: 1 week per Blood Potency<br /> Much like with the use of Oubliette, the Nosferatu marks their territory with their own Vitae. The amount of Vitae spent varies between five and twelve, depending on the size of the area they wish to mark. They then slumber. With these aspects, this Devotion seems very similar to the pinnacle of Obfuscate and indeed, a vampire that has marked an area with Halls of Madness benefits from all advantages of Oubliette. But this Devotion is so much more than that. It warps the vampire's territory, turning it... Surreal somehow. Like out of a bad dream. Shadows move when one traverses the Halls of Madness, a large figure brandishing a bloody knife can be seen, only for a second, only to disappear once one blinks. Faint laughter, or screams, can be heard echoing from far away. One opens a door and sees the inside of the room drenched in blood and recoils in horror, but it appears perfectly clean the next time they look. The Nosferatu may freely use Dread Presence, The Grand Delusion and Waking Nightmare on anyone inside the Halls of Madness. Furthermore, anyone that has spent more than a few minutes within Halls of Madness is on edge, nervous and jumpy. They suffer the Distracted Condition until they leave the area. Finally, if a mortal spends a full day and night in the Halls of Madness, she suffers an Integrity Breaking Point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. What is the xp cost?<br /> <br /> I'll have to look at the new nightmare levels again before I jump on the perequisites debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T10:51:10-07:00","id":632522,"title":"","content":"Considering that the first level of Nightmare is already about illusions, I think it is just a tweak in the usual Oubliette, covered more by the XP cost than by more than Nightmare 1.<br /> <br /> Of course, to use the higher level Nightmare powers allowed by the Devotion, you have to get them first. The Devotion just allow their use once you do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T10:54:13-07:00","id":632523,"title":"","content":"In 2e, Devotions are priced at about half the total prerequisite dots, give or take 1 experience if the power is especially versatile or especially narrow. So, you'd have to work out the prerequisites in order to determine the experience cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T10:59:25-07:00","id":632529,"title":"","content":"Another reason for me to reduce the requisites. I don't see this Devotion needing to be more than 2 or 3 XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T05:49:43-07:00","id":633356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/617841-dread-presence-question?p=632529#post632529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another reason for me to reduce the requisites. I don't see this Devotion needing to be more than 2 or 3 XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is Requiem devotions old and new have broken the known guidelines on what disciplines add to the mix.<br /> 2nd edition makes it worse. I still getting used to vigor + auspex lets you destroy obfuscate? What does adding fortitude to a psych discipline do?<br /> Does the 1st edition Nightmare and Vigor Nos devotions still work?<br /> Nightmare now has illusions which sort of crosses into obfuscate territory. Hence a point in your favor about lower perqs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}